<article class="env-lemma" id="01N3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01N3">Lemma <span data-tag="01N3">27.11.7</span>.</a> With hypotheses and notation as in Lemma <a href="/tag/01MY" data-tag="01MY">27.11.1</a> above. Assume there exists a $g \in A_0$ such that $\psi $ induces an isomorphism $A_ g \to B$. Then $U(\psi ) = Y$, $r_\psi : Y \to X$ is an open immersion which induces an isomorphism of $Y$ with the inverse image of $D(g) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_0)$. Moreover the map $\theta $ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
